 SELLER AND BUYER NEED TO EXERCISE CAUTION WHILE TRANSACTING AND ARE ADVISED TO VERIFY THE AUTHENTICITY OF LISTINGS AND COUNTERPARTIES. PNP WILL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY KIND OF LOSS/DAMAGE TO THE BUYER OR SELLER, INCLUDING CONSEQUENTIAL AND INCIDENTAL LOSSES AND DAMAGES. NO GUARANTEE IS PROVIDED ON ANY MISREPRESENTATION. IF USERS EXCHANGE THEIR CONTACTS ON THE PLATFORM, AND IF ANYTHING HAPPENS TO ONE USER DUE TO THE ACT OF THE OTHER USER, SUCH AS THEFT OR CHEATING, PNP WILL NOT BE RESPONSIBLE FOR THE SAME. PNP DOES NOT PROMOTE CRIMINAL ACTIONS &amp; FRAUD AND ANY USER INDULGING IN CRIMINAL ACTIVITIES IS DOING SO OUT OF THEIR OWN VOLITION. PNP DOES NOT GUARANTEE SPECIFIC RELIEF OR SPECIFIC PERFORMANCE OF ANY CONTRACT/TERMS THAT A BUYER AND SELLER ON ITS PLATFORM ENTER INTO. PNP OPERATES AS AN INTERMEDIARY PLATFORM, AS DEFINED UNDER SECTION 2(W) OF THE INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY ACT, 2000, AND IS GOVERNED BY THE PROVISIONS OF THE SAME.</strong></p><p>Listers/Potential buyers are encouraged to promptly report any inaccurate or inappropriate content. Despite diligent efforts to ensure accuracy, completeness, and currency of information in listings and advertisements, PNP cannot guarantee the same. Users are strongly advised to independently verify all details. Representations and depictions of listed items, including pictures and visuals, which may differ from the actual product and services. Users should verify information from relevant authorities and developers (if applicable) before making any decisions on purchase of Listed Items and/or Advertised Items. In addition to the foregoing, it is pertinent to mention here that the definitions provided under Section 2(47) and Section 2(11) of the Consumer Protection Act, 2019 ("CPA") are crucial in describing the parameters of unfair trade practices and deficiency in services, respectively. "Unfair Trade Practices" as defined in Section 2(47) of the CPA, encompass the adoption of unfair methods or deceptive trade practices for the sale, use, or supply of any goods or provision of any service, including false representation about the standards, quality, or grade of services and representations purporting to be warranties or guarantees of services. "Deficiency" in services, as per Section 2(11) of the CPA, encompasses any fault, imperfection, or shortcoming in the quality, nature, and manner of performance required by law or contract, including acts of negligence or omission resulting in loss or injury to the consumer. As an intermediary platform, PNP operates solely to facilitate the exchange of information between users and does not exercise control over the content of listings or the quality of services offered therein. Consequently, PNP neither promotes nor engages in unfair trade practices, nor can it be held liable for any deficiency in services as defined under the CPA. Users are hereby apprised that any grievances regarding unfair trade practices or deficiency in services pertaining to listings should be addressed directly with the owner of the respective listing. PNP assumes no responsibility for the actions or representations of users. Users are apprised that for any perceived unfair trade practices or deficiencies in services, the user can file consumer complaints directly against the owners of the listings.</p><h2>Limitations of Liability</h2><p><strong>IN NO EVENT SHALL PNP, ITS OFFICERS, DIRECTORS, EMPLOYEES, OR AGENTS, BE LIABLE FOR DIRECT, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR EXEMPLARY DAMAGES (EVEN IF PNP HAS BEEN ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES), RESULTING FROM ANY ASPECT OF YOUR USE OF THE PLATFORM OR THE SERVICE, INCLUDING WITHOUT LIMITATION WHETHER THE DAMAGES ARISE FROM USE OR MISUSE OF THE PLATFORM OR THE SERVICE, FROM INABILITY TO USE THE PLATFORM OR THE SERVICE, OR THE INTERRUPTION, SUSPENSION, MODIFICATION, ALTERATION, OR TERMINATION OF THE PLATFORM OR THE SERVICE. SUCH LIMITATION OF LIABILITY SHALL ALSO APPLY WITH RESPECT TO DAMAGES INCURRED BY REASON OF OTHER SERVICES OR PRODUCTS RECEIVED THROUGH OR ADVERTISED IN CONNECTION WITH THE PLATFORM OR THE SERVICE OR ANY LINKS ON THE PLATFORM, AS WELL AS BY REASON OF ANY INFORMATION, OPINIONS OR ADVICE RECEIVED THROUGH OR ADVERTISED IN CONNECTION WITH THE PLATFORM OR THE SERVICE OR ANY LINKS ON THE PNP SITE. THESE LIMITATIONS SHALL APPLY TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW.</strong></p><p><strong>YOU SPECIFICALLY ACKNOWLEDGE AND AGREE THAT PNP SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR USER SUBMISSIONS OR THE DEFAMATORY, OFFENSIVE, OR ILLEGAL CONDUCT OF ANY USER OR THIRD PARTY AND THAT THE RISK OF HARM OR DAMAGE FROM THE FOREGOING RESTS ENTIRELY WITH YOU.</strong></p><p>The platform is controlled and offered by PNP. PNP makes no representations or warranties that the platform is appropriate for use in other locations. Those who access or use the platform from other jurisdictions do so at their own volition and risk and are responsible for compliance with local law.</p><h2>Assignment</h2><p>These Terms, and any rights and licenses granted hereunder, may not be transferred or assigned by you but may be assigned by PNP without restriction. Any assignment or transfer by you shall be null and void.</p><h2>Ability to Accept Terms of Service</h2><p>You affirm that you are at least 18 years of age and are fully able and competent to enter into the terms, conditions, obligations, affirmations, representations, and warranties set forth in these Terms, and to abide by and comply with these Terms.</p><p>This Platform is intended only for adults and that you are eligible to contract as per applicable laws. If you are using/accessing this Platform as a representative of any person/entity, you acknowledge that you are legally authorized to represent that person/entity. Minors, i.e. users under 18 years of age, are only allowed to access the Platform with prior approval of their legal guardian. Minors are not allowed to use the Service. Minors under Indian law cannot enter into any contracts